condition_name: Peripheral Vascular Disease
condition_slug: peripheral-vascular-disease
source: NSTG 2022
introduction: "Chronic and progressive disease due to the atherosclerotic narrowing of the peripheral blood vessels. Commonly affects the peripheral arteries of the legs. Others peripheral vessels that may be affected are that of stomach, arms or head."
clinical_features[1]:
  - type: features
    features[6]: Hair loss on the feet and legs and brittle toenails,Intermittent claudication,Numbness in the legs.,Sores or ulcers on the legs and feet that take a long time to heal,Difficulty in finding a pulse in the leg or foot.,Erectile dysfunction
investigations[3]: Ankle Brachial Index(ABI),A pulse volume record,A vascular ultrasound
treatment:
  goals[3]: To reduce cardiovascular risk,To manage symptoms,To prevent limb loss.
  non_drug[2]: "Lifestyle modifications (cessation of smoking, exercise, healthy diet, care of feet)","Management of conditions, such as diabetes and high blood pressure"
  drug[6]: "Antiplatelet: Low-dose aspirin 81 to 325 mg/day",Clopidogrel 75 mg daily is an alternative,"Anticoagulant: heparin and warfarin are anticoagulant medications.","Phosphodiesterase III inhibitor: Cilostazol: 100 mg twice daily","Pentoxifylline: (To improves blood flow to the extremities)",Antihypertensives may to prevent strokes and heart attacks
  adverse_reactions_and_cautions[1]: "Headache, diarrhoea, and dizziness."
  supportive_measures[0]:
differential_diagnoses[5]: Deep venous thrombosis (DVT),Lumbar (intervertebral) disk disorders,Mechanical back pain,Septic thrombophlebitis,Superficial thrombophlebitis
complications[5]: Amputation,Poor wound healing.,Restricted mobility due to pain or discomfort.,Severe pain in the affected extremity.,Stroke
prevention[1]: "Advice against smoking, high cholesterol and high blood pressure"
other_investigations: null
definitive_treatment[3]: Revascularisation,Angioplasty,Artery by pass graft
prognosis: null